                        "review": "every single individual encounter is so unpredictable, and the game forces you into unrealistic split-second quickdraw situations so often, it ends up feeling like a game designed around a save state feature that it just doesn't have.\n\nso prepare to restart ten thousand times as your inaccurate gun, stupid partner, inexplicably chaotic civilians, unrealistic protocol, and the simple inconsistency of mechanics like doorways and melee fail you over and over again in every tight situation.\n\nmeanwhile the fearless and cunning amateur criminals perfectly triangulate your location from your first gunshot and set ambushes behind every door, almost every single one fully willing to upgrade their firearm or drug possession charge into double police homicide for some stupid reason.",
